 "technique": "kingcrimson",
 "means": "For every scored T-spin in the corpus (a T with an engine spin credit that cleared lines, inside the verified prefix, passing the reconstruction check), whether harddrop's King Crimson local shape stood around it: the lock's cells are the page's T stood up, nub toward the open side (as drawn, or mirrored), and every cell of the window around it — the well's wall, the overhang over the well, the TST slot, the STSD slot three rows under it and the wall on the open side — is filled or empty as drawn. The opportunity is a full T-spin Triple; every hit is followed to the next T lock to see whether the STSD the page draws next fired.",
 "not_eligible_because": "simulator output: which local shape a T went into is read off the vendored Triangle engine's boards, and nothing on the corpus side has a second implementation of it. No claim id, no badge, no figure in a report.",
 "caveat": "garbage is read as FILLED inside the window, and its hole columns are the engine's seeded-RNG columns, which disagree with the recorded ones (oracle-source.ts); a hit with garbage in its window is named in garbage_in_window for that reason. At a full TST the three cleared rows are entailed by the clear (NaiveClauseForced): the overhang above and the STSD slot below discriminate. Counts only, always N / M with the denominator.",
 "rules": [
  "opportunity: a T lock with spin \"full\" clearing 3 lines, at a 0-based lock index <= the verified index, whose board-before plus its cells makes exactly the rows the engine recorded clearing (the reconstruction check, counted exactly as opener-facts.json donation.check counts it)",
  "match: the lock's cells equal the variant's stood T under one translation (mirrored: columns reflected in the window), and every other window cell is filled (a piece or garbage) or empty as the page draws it; colour is never compared; cells outside the window are not read",
  "mirrored is tried only when as-drawn fails; a window leaving the board is no match (window_off_board)",
  "follow-up: the page's STSD slot (a second T stood up three rows under the TST's, nub toward the open side, every cell under the TST's cleared rows) carried through every clear and garbage insertion to the next T lock, each step verified against the engine's next board; fired iff that T is the slot and a scored full TSD",
  "controls: the same window at scored TSS, TSD, mini TSS and mini TSD; ablations no_must_empty, no_roof and t_overlap at the opportunity; orientation_baseline = opportunities whose T stands up"
 ],
